    "body": "Thanks, but I think this misunderstands the idea. It's not saying \"whenever you want to represent a single key, use double-kbd\". It's saying \"when you see double-kbd, that means that we're representing a single key inside the context of a larger string of user input\". The example in the section you linked to clarifies this, especially the \"such precision isn't necessary\" section.",
