    "body": "That's fair. Hixie also [mentioned in 2009](http://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2009Aug/0257.html) that the nested examples were \"basically aimed at the pedants who like to argue about exactly how to mark up particular semantics.\"\r\n\r\nSo I agree that either convention is defensible, however, shouldn't the source be consistent in the convention it uses, even if we don't change the user-facing Usage Samples section?",
