    "created_at": "2017-02-16T21:21:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-16T21:21:11Z",
    "body": "I don't think so... I just don't see any justification for `<kbd><kbd>x</kbd></kbd>`. I only see a reason to nest kbds if there's other intervening text, such as `<kbd>x <kbd>y</kbd> z</kbd>`.\r\n\r\nI think the source is very consistent in the convention it uses. It uses `<kbd>` to denote user input, and when there's a specific key input it wants to call out within `<kbd>`, it wraps that in a nested `<kbd>`. Can you explain why you think it's inconsistent?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
