    "updated_at": "2017-02-24T20:48:35Z",
    "body": "@domenic Sorry, missed the followup.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, in *every* other location that the spec, in its own markup, references a keypress, it uses two nested kbd tags. I can't link to the lines directly (GitHub complains that the file is too large), but as of current `master` (deffd672d8f03f9fa169a76a9cb5c4b5d2bc5235) they are:\r\n\r\n- L16598: `<kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>&larr; Left</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L16601: `<kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>&rarr; Right</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L16604: `<kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>&uarr; Up</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L16607: `<kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>&darr; Down</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L16612: `<kbd><kbd>j</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L16613: `<kbd><kbd>k</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L73136: `<kbd><kbd>shift</kbd>+<kbd>tab</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L73552-73553: `<kbd data-x=\"\"><kbd data-x=\"\">Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd data-x=\"\">Alt</kbd>+<kbd data-x=\"\">S</kbd></kbd>`\r\n- L73555: `<kbd><kbd>0</kbd></kbd>`\r\n\r\nSimilarly every other use of a single kbd tag in the spec represents typed user input:\r\n\r\n- L44273: `typed \"<kbd>spec.w</kbd>\"`\r\n- L47308: `typed \"<kbd>s</kbd>\"`\r\n- L47328: `entered \"<kbd>bob@example.net</kbd>\"`\r\n- L47329: `starting with \"<kbd>s</kbd>\"`\r\n- L47719: `typing \"<kbd>arrow</kbd>\" or \"<kbd>=></kbd>\"`\r\n- L47720-47722: `Typing \"<kbd>generator</kbd>\" or \"<kbd>*</kbd>\"`\r\n- L51078: `enters the word \"<kbd>three</kbd>\"`\r\n- L51081: `enters the email address \"<kbd>&nbsp;&nbsp;awesome@example.com</kbd>\"`\r\n- L73867: `typing \"<kbd>yellow&#x2423;&#x2423;ball</kbd>\"`\r\n- L111811: `enters \"<kbd>Kitty</kbd>\"`\r\n- L111812-111813: `enters \"<kbd dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">&#x644;&#x627;&nbsp;&#x623;&#x641;&#x647;&#x645;</kbd>\"`\r\n\r\nThis patch addresses the three instances where a single tag is inconsistently used to represent a keypress, instead of user input:\r\n\r\n- L73115: `the <kbd>tab</kbd> key`\r\n- L73135: `pressing <kbd>tab</kbd>`\r\n- L76059: `hitting the <kbd>Escape</kbd> key`\r\n\r\nDoes that make sense?\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
